\begin{corollary} \label{cor:bounded_variance}
 Assume that $\tilde{T}$ has uniformly bounded variance $\sigma^2$. Let $(x^n)_n$ be the sequence generated by the Halpern iteration~\eqref{halpern} with the stepsize $\beta_n=\frac{n}{n+1}$ and batch size $k_n = n^{4}$. Then, given $\varepsilon>0$, the Algorithm~\ref{alg_stochastic_halpern} finds $x^N$ such that $\EE(\norm{x^N-Tx^N})\le \varepsilon$ using at most $\tilde{O}(L^5\varepsilon^{-5})$ queries to the stochastic oracle, where $L=\max\{\mu \sigma, \dist(x^0, \Fix T)\}$.
\end{corollary}

