\begin{theorem} \label{thm:rate-nonexpansive}
 Let $(x^n)_n$ be the sequence generated by the Halpern iteration~\eqref{halpern} with the stepsize $\beta_n=\frac{n}{n+1}$. Assume that \eqref{H1} holds for some $\overline \kappa \geq 0$ and that $\sigma_n= \EE(\norm{U_n})$ is such that $\sum_{n=1}^N n\sigma_n =\tilde O(1)$. Then, given $\varepsilon>0$,  $\EE(\norm{x^N-Tx^N})\le \varepsilon$ for all $N \geq \bar N= \tilde{O}(\varepsilon^{-1})$ iterations.
