\subsection{Proof of Lemma~\ref{lem:sigma_explicito}} \label{apx:explicito}
Assuming that $\sum_{n=1}^N n\sigma_n \leq C \ln(N+1)$, the bound \eqref{bound-expected-nonexpansive} implies that
\begin{equation*} 
\EE(\norm{ x^N-Tx^N}) \le \frac{1}{N+1}\left( 3\bar{\kappa}+2C\right)\ln(N+1) \le \underbrace{(3\bar{\kappa} + 2C)}_{\leq\rho}\frac{\ln(N+1)}{N+1}, \end{equation*}
where we have used the rough bound $3\ln(N+1)\geq \sum_{n=1}^{N+1}\frac{1}{n}$ for all $N \geq 1$, in order to keep the estimates simple at the expense of some small factor.
